# The Generate and Judge Guide

Throughout Thinking Critically About AI, students build a Generate and Judge Guide that synthesizes their investigations, testing, reflections, and evidence about responsible AI use.

Unlike a traditional end-of-unit project completed all at once, students revisit and revise their guide throughout the unit. By the end of the unit, students produce a guide that combines:
* examples and evidence from AI investigations
* recommendations for responsible AI use
* reflections about context, judgment, and human responsibility

## Explore a Sample Guide

On the next level, you’ll explore a sample Generate and Judge Guide created from work across the unit.

<div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:10px; border-radius:10px; margin:15px 0px;">

**As you explore the sample project on the next level, look for:**
* How the student uses evidence and examples from earlier lessons
* Where the student makes nuanced or conditional recommendations about AI use
* How the student explains when human judgment matters
* How the project balances AI usefulness with risks and limitations

</div>


